[ti:Velvet Hour]
[ar:Odile Marchetti]
[al:After Hours]
[by:Vela demo — original lyrics]

[00:08.14]Velvet hour, the lamps go low
[00:12.20]Somebody's laughing down the hall
[00:16.27]The ice has melted in my glass
[00:20.34]And I don't mind it, not at all
[00:24.41]You hum the part the horn forgot
[00:28.47]I keep the time with my left hand
[00:32.54]The night is slow and I am slower
[00:36.61]Nothing here I need to understand
[00:40.68]Stay till the velvet hour's over
[00:44.75]Stay till the bar turns up the light
[00:48.81]We'll take the long way to the corner
[00:52.88]And call it morning, call it night
[00:56.95]Rain on the awning, soft and steady
[01:01.02]The pianist plays it like a prayer
[01:05.08]You ask me if I'm getting sleepy
[01:09.15]I say I'm only halfway there
[01:13.22]Stay till the velvet hour's over
[01:17.29]Stay till the bar turns up the light
[01:21.36]We'll take the long way to the corner
[01:25.42]And call it morning, call it night
